2-
3:On-call notes for the support log bundler. Keep this in sync with the code.
4-
5:## Why the archive steps use wildcards
6-
7-The log directories hold rotated files (`app.log`, `app.log.1`, `app.log.2.gz`)
8-alongside scratch files the collector leaves behind. Archive steps select what
9:they want with a wildcard rather than enumerating the directory, so that a new
10-rotation suffix does not need a code change.
11-
12-Some accounts have more than one collector writing into the same directory, and
--
17-
18-## Retention
19-
20:`cases.retention_days` is advisory. The cleanup job reads it; the bundler and
21-the exporter do not.
22-
23-## Where the case index comes from
24-
25-`cases` is written by the CRM sync job every fifteen minutes. Support agents
26:edit case fields in the CRM, so `ref`, `account` and `include_glob` are
27-whatever the CRM last handed us. Nothing in this repo writes to that table.
